                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbfb64b9-0613-3d50-9de6-943f9caea9b8",
                        "entry_id": "c04e1b71-28c8-3616-924f-fe643302363b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "beech"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "relational"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26127a33-b380-4143-aa09-f5ea090c4729",
                                "sense_id": "bbfb64b9-0613-3d50-9de6-943f9caea9b8",
                                "text": "Когда́ он вы́здоровел, его́, похуде́вшего и вы́росшего, увезли́ за грани́цу, сперва́ на бе́рег Адриати́ческого мо́ря, где он лежа́л на со́лнце в саду́, разы́грывая в уме́ па́ртии, что запрети́ть ему́ бы́ло невозмо́жно, зате́м — в неме́цкий куро́рт, где оте́ц води́л его́ гуля́ть по тропи́нкам, огоро́женным зате́йливыми бу́ковыми пери́лами.",
                                "translation": "Upon his recovery, a taller and thinner boy, he was taken abroad, at first to the Adriatic coast where he lay on the garden terrace in the sun and played games in his head, which nobody could forbid him, and then to a German resort where his father took him for walks along footpaths fenced off with twisted beech railings.",
                                "english": "Upon his recovery, a taller and thinner boy, he was taken abroad, at first to the Adriatic coast where he lay on the garden terrace in the sun and played games in his head, which nobody could forbid him, and then to a German resort where his father took him for walks along footpaths fenced off with twisted beech railings."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
